    "created_at": "2019-01-15T02:22:36Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-01-15T02:22:36Z",
    "body": "> It's predictable that \"load\" and \"DOMContentLoaded\" will never be logged\r\n\r\nRight, hence \"I was adding the listener too early\".  Adding the listeners after the open() call shows the interop issues.\r\n\r\nIs there a chance of that Chrome bug getting fixed?  To allow off-thread parsing it would be best if close() did not have normative sync behavior of any sort for things that can't happen until end of parsing (e.g. the readyState change and the DOMContentLoaded firing).",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
