    "created_at": "2019-01-15T02:24:00Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-01-15T02:24:00Z",
    "body": "(And to be clear, I am still investigating the various test fallout from implementing the spec's `document.open` behavior in Gecko, and the firing of the load event is one of the big issues; this used to be handled automatically-ish by the navigation-like behavior of `open()`.  I need to implement it somehow, but I am trying to figure out what the actual behavior is going to need to be.)",
